  "id": "cross-tolerance",
  "term": "cross-tolerance",
  "definition": "Cross-tolerance is when long-term use of one drug makes a person less responsive to the effects of other drugs that act in a similar way, such as other mu-receptor agonists. In this context, it can reduce physical dependence on those other drugs.",
